course: dictionary
lesson: 15223
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives six meanings for services, so you cannot just pick the first one you think of. Use the context, which is the other words in the sentence. «Our town has good public services, like buses, water and libraries.» The words public, buses and water tell you services means systems that supply things everyone needs.
explain: «We stopped at the services on the motorway to buy a sandwich and fill up with petrol.» Motorway, petrol and sandwich are the clues. Here services is a place beside the road where you can stop. Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence. Does "a place beside the road where you can stop" fit? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The ambulance and fire services arrived within minutes.» Ambulance and fire are the clues, so services here means the emergency services, the people who help when there is danger. Services is a plural noun, and its singular is service. Watch for that ending when you read.
fact: Services is a plural noun. Its singular form is service.
fact: «Emergency services» means the police, fire brigade, ambulance and coastguard.
fact: «Public services» means systems like water, electricity, buses and health care that everyone needs.
fact: «Motorway services» means a place beside a motorway with fuel, food and toilets (in the UK).
fact: «Goods and services»: goods are things people make and sell, and services are work done for people, such as cleaning or hairdressing.
exercise: «The ambulance and fire services arrived within minutes.» What do the services mean here? | *Emergency services, the people who help when there is danger | Cleaning and hairdressing | Places to buy food on a road trip | Church ceremonies
exercise: Which one is a service, not a good? | A bag of apples | *A haircut | A new bicycle | A bookcase
exercise: «We stopped at the services on the motorway for petrol and a cup of tea.» What are the services? | The armed forces | *A place beside the motorway with fuel and food | A church ceremony | Online apps and websites
test: «Our town's public services include water, electricity and buses.» What are public services? | Only the police and the fire brigade | Work done by one person for a single friend | *Systems that supply things everyone needs | Religious ceremonies
test: «The service in the old church began at ten o'clock.» What does service mean here? | Emergency help | *A religious ceremony | Work done for people | A place beside a motorway
exam: «Mum said, "Online services like banking apps are easy to use."» What do online services mean here? | Places beside the road | *Apps and websites you use on a computer or phone | Church ceremonies | Emergency calls to the police
